WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:03.000
-Now, Ice,
you're a man of many talents.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.405
You're an accomplished
actor, producer,

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.306
musician --
Grammy-winning musician.

00:00:07.306 --> 00:00:09.942
You're also --
You're also known for not being

00:00:09.942 --> 00:00:11.644
afraid to speak your mind

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:14.013
and for your no-holds-barred
commentary on Twitter.

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:16.816
So I thought we could go through
some of your tweets

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.852
and you could tell us
a little more

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:20.619
about your thoughts behind them.

00:00:20.619 --> 00:00:22.888
Is that okay?
Is that okay by you?

00:00:22.888 --> 00:00:24.657
-This should be good.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:27.026
-All right. Good.
Let's start with this one.

00:00:27.026 --> 00:00:28.528
This says...

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:31.164
"I remember when I said I had
breakfast at IHOP or Denny's.

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:32.832
MFs lost it.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:34.967
Like there's some Gucci egg
somewhere I should be eating.

00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:37.036
LOL. SMH."

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:39.338
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.338 --> 00:00:41.907
-I mean, yeah.
I mean, I eat at normal spots.

00:00:41.907 --> 00:00:44.744
I mean, breakfast is breakfast.
An egg is an egg.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:47.913
You know, like, where are you
supposed to eat breakfast?

00:00:47.913 --> 00:00:49.615
At Tiffany's or something?

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:51.217
Like, people bug out.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:53.686
If I say I go to Taco Bell,
they're like,

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:55.621
"You eat at Taco Bell?"

00:00:55.621 --> 00:00:57.424
I'm like, "I don't have, like,

00:00:57.424 --> 00:00:59.425
a Mexican chef fly in
to make me tacos.

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:01.394
This is how we eat tacos."
-Yeah. It tastes delicious.

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:02.929
Yeah, exactly.

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:06.665
"Bonus ice cold fact: you can't
change some of your friends

00:01:06.665 --> 00:01:09.469
so you're gonna have to change
some of your friends."

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.070
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:14.073
That one had me thinking
a little bit.

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:16.209
-I mean, some of your friends
won't grow up.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:18.544
Some of your friends
are still on that BS.

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:20.179
You know what I'm saying?
-Oh, I see.

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:22.715
-You gotta say, "You know,
I got to let you go, man."

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:25.017
-Oh, so you can't change
some of your friends

00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:27.420
so you're gonna have to "change"
some of your friends.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:30.089
Wow! Wow! I love it.

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:32.391
That's a Gucci egg.
That's a Gucci egg.

00:01:32.391 --> 00:01:34.427
-There you go. Exactly.

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:36.962
-[ Laughs ] I like this one.

00:01:36.962 --> 00:01:39.098
You said, "Don't worry about
what people think about you.

00:01:39.098 --> 00:01:40.800
Because they probably
don't think about you

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.368
that much anyway."

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:43.736
[ Applause ]

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.071
-That's true.
-Yeah.

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:46.905
-I mean, even when people
are gossiping,

00:01:46.905 --> 00:01:49.042
they'll pick somebody out
and they might talk about them

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:51.777
for five minutes,
but after they finish with that,

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:53.813
they go back to their life.
-Yeah.

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:56.482
-So they don't really have a lot
of time to think about you.

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:57.784
So don't worry about it.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.285
It's not something
they do often.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:01.020
And if someone's
doing you constantly,

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.723
then they have a problem,
not you.

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.524
-This is what I'm ta--
This is why I follow you.

00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:08.361
This is what I'm talking about.

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:09.896
Let's do a couple more here.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:12.798
"Whenever someone tries
to diss me by saying I'm old,

00:02:12.798 --> 00:02:15.468
I'm like, 'That's a fact.
Where's the insult?'"

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.470
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.772
-You know what I'm saying?
Aren't we all trying to get old?

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:23.609
I mean, what's the --
what's the alternative?

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:24.810
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.712
So I'm happy every day I live.

00:02:26.712 --> 00:02:28.548
I've just turned 63.

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.682
You know, I'm still thin in the
waist, handsome in the face.

00:02:30.682 --> 00:02:32.185
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:33.485
-That's what
I'm talking about, bud.

00:02:33.485 --> 00:02:35.588
-That's what I'm talking about.

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:38.757
-Last one here says,
"Twitter is like a friend

00:02:38.757 --> 00:02:40.326
I talk to sometimes...

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.395
that has a million heads.
LOL."

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:45.031
That's the truth.
-Yeah.

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:47.566
If you do like I do, I'm on --

00:02:47.566 --> 00:02:50.469
My Twitter name is
FINALLEVEL.com.

00:02:50.469 --> 00:02:52.238
And I talk to my fans.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.908
I use Twitter sometimes
to get answers,

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:58.645
and I get feedback from them,
so I can put a question out

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:00.113
and I'll get a thousand answers.

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:01.514
First thing, you got to get

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:03.249
all the dummies
off of your Twitter feed

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.217
so that you can have a real line

00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:08.154
of, you know, information
moving back and forth.

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:11.691
But, you know, I got --
I get rid of them real quick.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:14.226
I've got a hair-trigger
block button. You know?

00:03:14.226 --> 00:03:15.961
And, also, I like using mute.

00:03:15.961 --> 00:03:17.830
If you're new to Twitter,
use mute,

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.999
because then the person
doesn't know they blocked,

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:22.501
and then they just yell
into the abyss.

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.804
They yell into
the void of Twitter

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:26.438
thinking you're
still hearing them.

00:03:26.438 --> 00:03:28.774
-Ice-T. I love you, man.
Best to the family.

00:03:28.774 --> 00:03:30.743
Come back whenever
you want to, pal.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:33.212
Congrats on everything, man.
I'm happy for you.

00:03:33.212 --> 00:03:34.914
Ice-T, everybody.

